<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anambra River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Omambala River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anambra River, also called the Omambala, is a river of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> that flows into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> near Onitsha. Its valley is the setting of Nri traditions, which say the culture hero Eri descended from the sky near its banks. The river gave its name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anambra-state">Anambra State</a>, created in 1976, and its floodplains are important for farming and fishing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anambra-river.jpg" alt="Anambra River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ndukwe victor izuchukwu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amamba.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
